BYD wants to be the world’s top automaker by 2030
Quoting @leixing77
Key messages from Wang Chuanfu at BYD's annual general meeting:
We want to maintain growth in the next 3-5 years, striving to become global No. 1 in vehicle output & sales by 2030;
Vehicle export this year should exceed prior target of 1.6 million units;
Vehicle sales this year are dependent on second-gen blade/flash charging battery production bottleneck, which is ramping at about 20,000-30,000 units increase per month, expect output to jump in 2027;
Ready and preparing for rollout of Level 3 automated driving once policies and regulations are in place.
Recap: January-May total vehicle sales were 1.4 million units, down 20%, exports were 614,000 units, up 64.7%.
